b11a810914f52fd74619c734aa2f59536","file":"preprints/Finite-generation-for-the-Kn-local-sphere-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":13,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2714c9154a23c2e6d57557ffa7873c77b97ea5c1a5821843c0fbae407d043707","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Finite-generation-for-the-Kn-local-sphere-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a7165e61876f31924536899b1cf3388b11a810914f52fd74619c734aa2f59536","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Finite-generation-for-the-Kn-local-sphere-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L13"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\\label{thm:descent-integral}\nFor every prime $p$, every integer $n\\geq 1$, and every integer $t$,\nthe $\\Zp$-module\n\\[\n                 \\pi_t L_{K(n)}S_p^\\wedge\n\\]\nis finitely generated. Equivalently, for every finite $p$-local\nspectrum $F$, the module $\\pi_t L_{K(n)}F$ is finitely generated\nover $\\Zp$ in every integer degree $t$."}
